        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(infra): consolidate bounded HTTP body reads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nBounded HTTP response reads were owned by the private media package even though the primitive is transport infrastructure used across agents, gateway, plugins, media, and provider flows. That left HTTP lifecycle behavior coupled to a media-domain package and duplicated its ownership alongside request-body handling.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMoves the existing exact Web `Response` byte-limit implementation into `src/infra/http-body.ts`, preserving overflow, idle-timeout, cancellation, reader-lock, fallback, decoding, and caller-provided error behavior. Core callers and the existing Plugin SDK facades now use the infra owner; JSON/text interpretation, status handling, retries, logging, and provider policy remain with callers. The private `@openclaw/media-core/read-response-with-limit` subpath and its build/alias scaffolding are removed.\n\nThe deprecated `plugin-sdk/infra-runtime` barrel is pinned to its pre-existing request-body exports so the relocated response readers remain available only through the focused `response-limit-runtime` and existing `media-runtime` surfaces.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. Maintainers and plugin authors keep the same supported Plugin SDK response-limit APIs, with one canonical core owner for bounded HTTP request and response reads.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact head: `b5ed973ce800463d49e27067c620682f4c7f6657`.\n- CI failure triage: `checks-node-compact-small-whole-2` on the prior head failed deterministically in `test/scripts/plugin-sdk-surface-report.test.ts`; the relocation made existing package-backed exports source-resolvable and accidentally leaked two response readers through deprecated `infra-runtime`. This was branch-caused, not flaky or unrelated.\n- Fix proof: `infra-runtime` now preserves its exact prior request-body surface; source budgets are pinned to 10,414 public exports, 5,230 callable exports, and a reduced 212 wildcard re-exports.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/plugin-sdk-surface-report.test.ts src/infra/http-body.test.ts src/infra/http-body.response.test.ts src/plugins/sdk-alias.test.ts src/plugins/contracts/plugin-sdk-subpaths.test.ts` — 4 shards passed, 126 tests.\n- `pnpm build` — passed, including tsdown, Plugin SDK export checks, runtime postbuild, and Control UI build.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kwndqmfeptbxbstfh2t85yy0` — `pnpm check:changed` passed full typecheck, core/extensions/scripts lint, guards, and runtime import-cycle checks.\n- Testbox Actions run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28691540557\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --prompt-file tmp/notes.md --stream-engine-output` — clean; no accepted/actionable findings, correctness confidence 0.98.\n- Production/config diff remains net-negative.\n",
